CAT = "cpaaudRisk"; SEG = "RSK"
Q = [
("Under AU-C 240, which fraud risk is presumed in every audit and may be rebutted?",
 "Improper revenue recognition", ["Theft of petty cash funds", "Payroll fraud by supervisors", "Kickbacks paid to purchasing staff"],
 "The auditor presumes a fraud risk in revenue recognition. If it is rebutted, the reasons are documented. Management override is the risk that cannot be rebutted."),
("Because management override of controls is a risk in every audit, the auditor must:",
 "Test journal entries", ["Confirm all receivables", "Count all inventory", "Test every control"],
 "Responses to management override include testing journal entries and other adjustments, reviewing estimates for bias and evaluating the business rationale for significant unusual transactions."),
("In the fraud triangle, a sales manager whose bonus depends on hitting a quarterly target illustrates:",
 "Incentive", ["Opportunity", "Rationalization", "Capability"],
 "The three conditions are incentive or pressure, opportunity, and attitude or rationalization. A bonus tied to a target is an incentive. Capability belongs to the later fraud diamond, not the triangle."),
("Weak controls over cash receipts in a small office, where one clerk handles the mail and the deposits, illustrate which fraud condition?",
 "Opportunity", ["Incentive", "Rationalization", "Pressure"],
 "Opportunity exists when controls are absent or ineffective, as when one person handles both the receipt and the recording of cash."),
("When testing journal entries for fraud, which entry is most suspicious?",
 "Round sums posted after year-end", ["Recurring monthly depreciation entries", "Automated payroll postings", "System-generated sales entries"],
 "Entries made at the end of a period or after close, with round numbers, little explanation or to seldom-used accounts carry higher fraud risk."),
("The auditor identifies a misstatement that results from fraud by a junior clerk and is not material. The auditor should:",
 "Tell an appropriate level of management", ["Ignore it, as it is immaterial", "Report it to the police first", "Withdraw from the engagement immediately"],
 "Evidence of fraud, even immaterial, is brought to the attention of an appropriate level of management, at least one level above those involved."),
("Under AU-C 250, laws such as tax and pension laws that directly affect amounts in the statements require the auditor to:",
 "Obtain evidence of compliance", ["Perform no specific work", "Rely on management only", "Report each law to the SEC"],
 "For laws with a direct effect on material amounts and disclosures, the auditor obtains sufficient appropriate evidence of compliance. For other laws, procedures are limited to identifying noncompliance."),
("When auditing an accounting estimate, which approach is acceptable under SAS 143?",
 "Developing an auditor's range", ["Accepting management's figure", "Using last year's estimate", "Asking the client's banker"],
 "SAS 143 allows testing how management made the estimate, developing an auditor's point estimate or range, or using events up to the report date."),
("A retrospective review of last year's estimates against actual outcomes is mainly performed to look for:",
 "Management bias", ["Sampling error", "Cutoff errors", "IT access issues"],
 "Comparing prior estimates with their outcomes helps the auditor detect a pattern of management bias and judge the reliability of the current process."),
("Which procedure is most likely to uncover related party transactions not disclosed by management?",
 "Reading board minutes", ["Confirming receivables", "Recomputing depreciation", "Observing inventory"],
 "Minutes, contracts, bank confirmations of guarantees and large unusual transactions often reveal related parties management has not identified."),
("Before using the work of a management's specialist as evidence, the auditor evaluates the specialist's competence, capabilities and:",
 "Objectivity", ["Fee arrangement", "Firm size", "Office location"],
 "The auditor evaluates the competence, capabilities and objectivity of a management's specialist, obtains an understanding of the work, and evaluates its appropriateness as evidence."),
("An auditor's specialist values a complex asset. The auditor's report of a nonissuer refers to the specialist only when:",
 "The opinion is modified for it", ["The specialist is from an outside firm", "The valued asset is material", "Management asks for the reference"],
 "The auditor does not refer to an auditor's specialist in an unmodified opinion. A reference may be made when relevant to explaining a modification, stating that it does not reduce the auditor's responsibility."),
("Before using the work of internal auditors, the external auditor evaluates their objectivity, competence and whether they apply:",
 "A systematic, disciplined approach", ["Help from outside audit firms", "The same fee as the external auditor", "Statistical sampling on every test"],
 "The internal audit function's objectivity, competence and use of a systematic and disciplined approach, including quality control, determine whether its work can be used."),
("Internal auditors may give the external auditor direct assistance, but not on tasks that:",
 "Involve significant judgment", ["Use external confirmations", "Are performed at year-end", "Involve the cash accounts"],
 "Internal auditors may not perform procedures that involve significant judgment, relate to high risks where more than limited judgment is needed, or cover work they were involved in."),
("In a group audit, the group auditor decides to make reference to a component auditor's report. The group auditor's report must:",
 "State the share it audited", ["Name the component audit firm", "Disclaim on that component", "Attach the component's report"],
 "When reference is made, the report indicates the magnitude of the portion of the statements audited by the component auditor. The other firm is not named without its permission. SAS 149 renamed the group engagement team the group auditor but kept this option."),
("A client is a defendant in a large lawsuit. That is mainly a risk to which assertion of its liabilities?",
 "Completeness", ["Existence", "Rights and obligations", "Cutoff"],
 "An unrecorded or understated contingent liability is a completeness risk. The auditor's inquiry of legal counsel addresses it."),
("Under the Uniform Guidance, major programs for a single audit are chosen using:",
 "A risk-based approach", ["Random selection", "The largest program only", "The auditee's choice"],
 "The auditor classifies programs as Type A or Type B by expenditure size and applies a risk-based approach to determine which are audited as major programs."),
("In a single audit, the auditor's opinion on compliance is given for:",
 "Each major program", ["Every federal program", "Only Type B programs", "The largest grant only"],
 "Under the Uniform Guidance, the auditor gives an opinion on compliance for each major program, along with a report on internal control over compliance."),
("An entity sells goods with an unusual bill-and-hold arrangement near year-end. This raises the risk of:",
 "Premature revenue recognition", ["Understated inventory quantities", "Overstated operating expenses", "Unrecorded accounts payable"],
 "Bill-and-hold sales near period end are a classic way to accelerate revenue, so the auditor scrutinizes whether control has transferred."),
("An auditor of a nonissuer suspects that a fraud involves senior management. The auditor should communicate it to:",
 "Those charged with governance", ["The SEC directly and at once", "The local press and media", "The lowest level of staff involved"],
 "Fraud involving senior management, or causing a material misstatement, is communicated to those charged with governance. Outside reporting is limited by confidentiality, except in specific cases."),
]
